Detail for C1.e.  RIVAL, S = 1: on-path turns in all 144 cases: 1008.  Turns that start
with twin c > 0: 0.  Sabotage events on the path: 0.  So on the path the sabotage
statement is never put to the test; C1.f and C1.g test it at every node off the path.
Detail for C1.c.  RIVAL, G = 3: turns with k > 0, as (turn - T, mover, k), over all 72 cases:
  turn T+0, mover B, k = 1: 72 cases
Definition used in C1.f and C1.g: cap_binds = yes when the mover has more effort units
than free cap room in the twin before any sabotage (1 + c_mover > Cmax - c_twin).
Then a sabotage frees room for one more general unit.

